WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.410
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:04.360
SPEAKER 1: So you're
developing an app.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:07.750
And of course, that app is
innovative and groundbreaking.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:09.190
It has huge potential.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.530
And if it's as
successful as you expect,

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:15.750
it may one day exceed the
limits of traditional systems.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.560
You'll need a
NoSQL database that

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.890
is fast, simple to maintain,
and scales from gigabytes

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.330
to petabytes with no downtime.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.990
That's where Google Cloud
Bigtable comes into play.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.240
Cloud Bigtable is a
fully managed service,

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.280
meaning you can
concentrate on your app

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.380
instead of tuning your database.

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.450
With its unique
combination of low latency

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.240
and high throughput,
Cloud Bigtable

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.040
can scale to reliably
handle massive workloads

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.800
at lightning-fast speeds,
and up to millions

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.670
of operations per second with
no reconfiguration downtime.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.770
Customers are using
Cloud Bigtable today

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.310
for a range of applications,
from real-time ad analytics

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:53.290
all the way to tracking
millions of readings

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.690
from thousands of IoT sensors.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:58.840
And because Cloud Bigtable
is compatible with industry

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.260
standard tools like
HBase, Hadoop, and Google

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.510
BigQuery and Cloud
Dataflow, it means

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:08.920
it's easy to put all that
data to work for your app.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:12.460
Google Cloud Bigtable-- the
super fast, highly scalable,

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:16.612
NoSQL database your app
needs today and tomorrow.

